that they don't know how to take effective

4
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:25,140
notes as they listen.

5
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,020
Let's take the first question in the previous

6
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:30,840
exercise to see how we can navigate the

7
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:33,020
correct answers in all the options.

8
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,360
You can see that the speaker will mention

9
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:39,480
the animals in the options, however the order

10
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:41,800
they are mentioned in the audio will not

11
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,200
be A,B,C,D,E.

12
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:44,800
It will be mixed up.

13
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:47,900
The best strategy is to take quick notes

14
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:50,600
next to each option as you hear it.

15
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:52,940
Now let's go through my note.

16
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:55,360
The first animal mentioned is the penguin.

17
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,300
My note says average popularity.

18
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:00,380
This is option A.

19
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,459
We can cross this out because we need

20
00:01:03,459 --> 00:01:05,180
to hear about the most popular animals.

21
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:07,640
Next we hear about the giraffe.

22
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,500
The speaker says it was still quite popular.

23
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:13,260
This is option D and we can also

24
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:15,480
cross it out because quite popular isn't the

25
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,700
same as most popular.

26
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,300
Then we have option E, the tiger.

27
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,080
The note for this is came in a

28
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:22,620
close second.

29
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Close second is definitely one of the top

30
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,020
ranks so we should consider this a possible

31
00:01:28,020 --> 00:01:28,980
correct answer.

32
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:33,200
After that is the monkey, option B.

33
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:36,040
The note says it was near the top.

34
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:39,240
Again we will cross this out because near

35
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:41,420
the top is not at the top.

36
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:45,460
Finally we hear about the lion, option C.

37
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:49,040
The speaker says it was more popular than

38
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,420
anything else.

39
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:54,480
This phrase clearly means it was number one

40
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:57,100
so we will choose this answer.

41
00:01:57,680 --> 00:02:00,460
Normally you might get confused between two options

42
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:03,380
like E, tiger with the note a close

43
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:06,900
second and B, monkey with the note near

44
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:07,600
the top.

45
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:11,080
These phrases can sound similar when you are

46
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:14,100
listening quickly but if you take clear notes

47
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:16,780
as I've done you can see that a

48
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:20,280
close second is a top rank while near

49
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:21,760
the top is not.

50
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:25,340
This helps you confidently choose the correct answers.

51
